    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A post office has operated in Bejou since 1906, anchoring the community for over a century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bejou%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Bejou grew into a railroad village in 1904 when the Soo Line extended its tracks through the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.lakesnwoods.com/Bejou.htm"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Water from Bejou flows west into Marsh Creek, a tributary of the Wild Rice River that feeds the Red River watershed.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
